{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075493-beyond-vitae-willpower-or-integrity","id":1075493,"title":"Beyond Vitae: Willpower or Integrity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-09T09:00:30-07:00","id":1075493,"title":"Beyond Vitae: Willpower or Integrity","content":"Hello. I am building a custom template for my ancient eras game. It's a combo between vampire and the old 1st edition Purified. My game is meant to be a powerful one as the characters are essentially fledgling gods on earth.<br /> <br /> One of the abilities they gain is an enhanced blush of life which makes them nigh unstoppable save versus silver which causes agg. This blush of life is sustained on a daily basis like normal vampire abilities except I want it to draw on the vampire theme.<br /> <br /> Im currently going with so far; They can free themselves of the vampire curse for max days equal to their humanity, with a resource they must take, like vitae, to represent each day they can cheat the curse. <br /> <br /> If we take integrity, it costs 2 xp to recover it, lowers that human's morality and has a cost for any 'player' to take all of someone's integrity as it becomes a sin, like killing.<br /> <br /> The idea here is that the vampire steals a living mortals integrity to sustain its own unnatural state of life.<br /> <br /> What do you think; Willpower points/dots or Integrity dots taken from the mortal. Its a powerful effect and I feel like integrity is a better choice but I'd like advice and even some suggestions. <br /> <br /> I can explain more if needed as well. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T12:34:33-07:00","id":1075544,"title":"","content":"Think bigger. Drink their soul and digest it for fuel. Literally; instead of drawing upon Vitae, you can drink the soul of a mortal human. Tick off a box on your resource pool, and now they have no soul, with all the fun consequences that result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T18:28:15-07:00","id":1076226,"title":"","content":"You could also have an interesting effect if you do something like Demon's cover pacts, except you gain a certain number of days for level of &quot;cover&quot; you take. You are literally stealing chucks of people's very existence to feed yourself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:40:36-07:00","id":1076286,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for something that will have a visible, mechanical effect for the players' interaction with NPCs, Willpower is the marginally better choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T06:42:50-07:00","id":1076448,"title":"","content":"All hail the Ordo Dracul!<br /> <br /> Ahem<br /> <br /> Do the players / characters even know what they take? Fluff it as psuedo Diablerie and give it humanity checks. Maybe make it inflict Soulless instead of taking a trait. Otherwise don't worry about what it takes from NPCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:44:49-07:00","id":1076485,"title":"","content":"Yeah: stealing Integrity is fine and all, but what is actually being stolen? Soul bits? --That would work, and if the individual is drained to zero they are given the Soulless condition. If not... well they're left an unstable, broken wretch in short order as the underpinnings of their mind are shredded.<br /> <br /> From a Humanity perspective this would be as bad as killing them. Possibly worse. <br /> <br /> And yes, Willpower is a directly applicable pool to steal from as well, since it generally represents &quot;alternate magic energy&quot; from a mechanical point of view. <br /> <br /> Ordo would love to develop feeding mechanisms feasting on both sources to supplement blood. That would be... efficient.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:36:36-07:00","id":1084010,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses everyone. I did decide to go with willpower. Basically as my players need, they draw willpower from victims to sustain their unnatural state. Each stolen 'dot' of willpower provides them with 24 hours worth of supercharged life. They are free of the curse's effect on Fire and Sunlight, appear as human to all forms of investigation and gain Garou healing while this state persists (all bashing and lethal are healed each TURN). <br /> <br /> The players can retain stored days equal to their willpower stat. Should they steal away all willpower dots from a subject, they face a breaking point as well as the target gaining the Soulless condition. <br /> <br /> As a balance for the gains here, the players suffer the same Silver weakness that werewolves/shifters do, stopping their healing factor. Also, while the are 'human' they ARE human; meaning the body requires food, water and sleep. We have not come across illness, disease, poison and the more rare damage forms but so far, this works great.<br /> <br /> My players are however topping off before killing a foe in battle but its allowed as long as they don't take ALL the dying mortal's willpower dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}